From 06996b43a5f9eea5816b4cf08d4f71e17e9305e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zahary Karadjov <zahary@agent-harbor.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:27:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] test(vm2): step records, the upstream ExecutionEvent seam,
 and the timing modes

Extends the AVM_DIFFERENTIAL driver with four argv-selected modes so the
per-instruction execution observer can be compared the way M8 compares tree
roots: per record, native against wasm, rather than by count.

  steps       one line per executed instruction -- context id, pc, opcode,
              cumulative l2/da gas and contract address -- for eight programs,
              plus the flag-off/flag-on facts the observer promises (steps
              absent when off, the result otherwise unchanged, the count equal
              to total_instructions_executed).
  events      the SAME fields taken from upstream's existing per-instruction
              seam: collect_hints = true, then
              AvmSimulationHelper::simulate_for_witgen(hints), whose
              EventEmitter<ExecutionEvent> is where the events actually
              materialise. AvmSimAPI::simulate(collect_hints = true) does NOT
              return them -- simulate_for_hint_collection_internal instantiates
              simulate_for_witgen_internal with NoopEventEmitters -- so the
              no-patch fallback costs hint collection AND a re-simulation.
  bench       the untraced loop, naming nothing the observer patch adds.
  benchsteps  traced against untraced, interleaved inside one process.

`bench` names nothing new on purpose, and the whole file guards its use of the
new API on __has_include of the interface header, so the identical source
compiles in a tree that does not carry the observer patch. That is what makes
the disabled-costs-nothing comparison a comparison rather than a skip.

An eighth program is added for the step modes only: it jumps past the end of
its own bytecode, so instruction fetching throws before the opcode is known and
the observer must report LAST_OPCODE_SENTINEL. `burn` covers the other
exceptional shape (out of gas, opcode known) and `revert` a non-exceptional
halt.

With no arguments the driver is unchanged: M8's transcript still has its 1,308
ordinary lines and M8's seven checks still pass on this tree.
